---
machine:
  type: controlplane
  nodeLabels:
    topology.kubernetes.io/zone: dmf-u
  install:
    diskSelector:
      model: Samsung SSD 870
    # 2026-07-25: RTX 3090 arrived, tested in the AOOSTAR AG02 dock (ASMedia ASM2464
    # bridge) - never stable, every attempt failed within 9-47s (pciehp hotplug command
    # 0x1038 timeout or earlier). thunderbolt.host_reset=0 was the only kernel arg that
    # helped at all; pci=realloc,assign-busses/pcie_aspm=off/pcie_port_pm=off all made it
    # worse and were reverted the same day. See schematic.yaml.j2 for full history.
    # 2026-07-28: swapped to a PELADN Link S-3 dock (Intel Barlow Ridge JHL9480 TB5
    # controller, not ASMedia) - RTX 3090 enumerated cleanly and held the link with zero
    # disconnects while running the baseline schematic, far more stable than any AG02
    # attempt. First eGPU-schematic attempt (NVIDIA driver extensions) was reverted the
    # same day: `ext-nvidia-persistenced` blocks the entire boot on
    # /sys/bus/pci/drivers/nvidia existing, which only appears after a *successful*
    # nvidia.ko load - and nvidia.ko doesn't register-and-wait for a device to show up
    # later, it actively probes for a GPU at insmod time and hard-fails (ENODEV) if none
    # is present yet. Forcing it via machine.kernel.modules produced an infinite retry
    # loop when the dock wasn't linked up yet at that point in boot. The correct fix
    # (a machine.udev.rules entry triggering modprobe on the PCI hotplug "add" event,
    # instead of machine.kernel.modules) is still pending - not yet added.
    # Second attempt, same day: retrying the eGPU schematic with thunderbolt.host_reset=0
    # and nvidia.NVreg_OpenRmEnableUnsupportedGpus=1 both commented out in
    # schematic.yaml.j2, to isolate whether either was contributing to the instability.
    # No machine.kernel.modules block this time either.
    image: factory.talos.dev/installer/7d56465fc23be23c5c2f2bcb9f604592ff0b781241406cba8b30e9b1dc4f70b7:v1.13.7 # eGPU schematic, thunderbolt.host_reset=0 + nvidia unsupported-gpu flag both disabled - see `just talos gen-schematic-id-egpu`
    wipe: false
  kernel:
    modules:
      # Third attempt, same day: the official Talos NVIDIA GPU doc recommends exactly
      # this block (all 4 modules, including nvidia_drm this time). The earlier attempt
      # with this same config produced an infinite retry loop because the dock wasn't
      # connected at boot - nvidia.ko probes for a GPU at insmod time and hard-fails if
      # none is present, it doesn't register-and-wait. Retrying now with the dock already
      # connected and the link confirmed stable before the reboot, so modprobe should
      # succeed on the first attempt instead of looping.
      - name: nvidia
      - name: nvidia_uvm
      - name: nvidia_drm
      - name: nvidia_modeset
---
apiVersion: v1alpha1
kind: HostnameConfig
hostname: k8s-2
